{"requirements":[{"id":"tmp-hardening-persistence","requirement":"Mount /tmp with nosuid, nodev, and noexec, with the settings surviving reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before the change, /tmp was part of the root filesystem. Before restart it was an active, enabled tmpfs with all three options; after a confirmed boot-ID change it remained mounted with nosuid,nodev,noexec, mode 1777, working I/O, blocked direct execution, and blocked device-node access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f063f7d04ce424f","cmd-841f32e82a43439e","cmd-f2347d07e58a4c50","cmd-51ceee3f6fa54054","cmd-733bf64f8b264861","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"dev-shm-hardening-persistence","requirement":"Mount /dev/shm with nosuid, nodev, and noexec, with the settings surviving reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before the change, /dev/shm lacked noexec. Before restart it had all three required options and valid persistent configuration; after the confirmed reboot it retained those options, mode 1777, working I/O, blocked direct execution, and blocked device-node access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f063f7d04ce424f","cmd-841f32e82a43439e","cmd-f2347d07e58a4c50","cmd-51ceee3f6fa54054","cmd-733bf64f8b264861","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The task-related mutations were focused and coherent: persistent mount configuration, live activation, and the required reboot. Temporary execution, I/O, and device-node probes were removed. The two failed commands occurred while the node was restarting and show no unwanted mutation. Services, sockets, and package health recovered cleanly. The only minor residue is the retained /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening rollback copy created during configuration; it is low-risk and operationally useful, but remained after completion. No other unnecessary mutations were identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6c5d29173c64410","cmd-5a7f474ad778436b","cmd-53fb6886d18c4058","cmd-f2347d07e58a4c50","cmd-733bf64f8b264861","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both required mounts were hardened with nosuid,nodev,noexec and directly verified after a real reboot. The provider restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity corroborated by the lifecycle snapshot, and recovered system and mount functionality.","limitations":["The nosuid property is directly established by the kernel-reported mount options after reboot, but there was no separate privilege-transition test demonstrating suppression of setuid execution; noexec also prevents direct execution on these mounts.","The lifecycle inventory does not inspect /etc, so it cannot independently characterize the retained fstab backup beyond the executor command that created it."]}
